# Building the Epimone .deb

## Canonical build (debhelper + Meson) — recommended, use on the Kali VM

Install the build dependencies, then build from the repo root:

    sudo apt install debhelper meson ninja-build pkgconf \
        libgtk-4-dev libadwaita-1-dev libvte-2.91-gtk4-dev libglib2.0-dev
    dpkg-buildpackage -b -us -uc

This drives the Meson build through `debian/rules` (`dh $@ --buildsystem=meson`)
and writes `../epimone_<version>_<arch>.deb`. `-b` = binary-only, `-us -uc` =
don't sign. Shared-library dependencies are computed by `dh_shlibdeps` from the
build host's libraries, so run it **on the target distro** (Kali) for correct
version floors.

## Fallback build (no debhelper) — Meson + dpkg-dev only

For hosts without `debhelper`:

    sh debian/build-deb-nohelper.sh

Produces `epimone_<version>_<arch>.deb` in the repo root. Same install layout
and (on the same host) same dependencies as the debhelper build.

## Install on the Kali VM (amd64)

    sudo apt install ./epimone_0.1.0-1_amd64.deb

apt resolves the runtime dependencies. Launch from the app grid ("Epimone") or
run `epimone`.

## Architecture

This build targets **amd64**. For an **arm64** build later: build on an arm64
host (or cross-build), change nothing in `debian/control`'s `Architecture: amd64`
line to `arm64` (or use `any`), and rebuild — `dh_shlibdeps` recomputes the
correct arch-specific dependencies. No source or packaging-logic changes are
needed; the layout and dependency *names* are arch-independent.
